From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaszhongsj <lucaszhongsj@foxmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:14:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] host/touch: map a touch on a wide picture back onto the
 centred interface

A touch was passed through in the picture's own coordinates. On a wider-than-
16:9 picture the interface stays centred at its 16:9 size, so a tap landed
left of the control it was on, further off towards the edges.

hle_touch.c now maps the point through the picture's shape against the
interface's: a touch outside the centred interface is clamped onto it, and one
inside is scaled into it. The shape comes from dm_fps_state, which loader.c
defines; the definition is weak here so a unit test that links hle_touch.c
alone sees NULL and every touch passes through unmapped.

Checked: the mapping is unit-tested at 16:9 (unchanged) and at a wider shape.
(cherry picked from commit 22d58ec470721319fdc0de8f524a5e801f11c7e8)

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#2609
Reason: A wider-than-16:9 iPhone picture keeps its own shape, its touches land on the control they touch, and Animal Crossing: New Horizons refreshes the projections it cached at 16:9
Issue: none

---
 dm/host/hle_touch.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dm/host/hle_touch.c b/dm/host/hle_touch.c
index 8e6fdfe0..3baa3503 100644
--- a/dm/host/hle_touch.c
+++ b/dm/host/hle_touch.c
@@ -17,18 +17,31 @@ static struct { int down, pend; float x, y; } g_gf[16];   // the gesture recogni
 static pthread_mutex_t g_tl = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
 static int64_t g_tsamp; static uint64_t g_tlast_ns;
 
+// On a picture wider than 16:9 the game's interface keeps a 16:9 projection (view.s's Lscreen_projection scales the layout projection's x by
+// (16/9)/r), so it is drawn centred across that fraction of the width while the picture itself fills the screen. The front end normalises a
+// touch on the whole picture, so map it back onto that centred rectangle: a control is hit where it is drawn, and the screen's edges reach the
+// interface's edges (a touch outside it clamps there). 16:9 and taller pictures are left alone.
+__attribute__((weak)) uint8_t *dm_fps_state;   // loader.c defines it; a unit test that links only this file has no frame step page, and NULL means 16:9
+static float ui_x(float x) {
+    if (!dm_fps_state) return x;
+    float r; memcpy(&r, dm_fps_state + 0x58, 4);
+    if (!(r > 16.0f / 9.0f)) return x;
+    float v = 0.5f + (x - 0.5f) / ((16.0f / 9.0f) / r);
+    return v < 0 ? 0 : v > 1 ? 1 : v;
+}
 static void touch_apply(const dm_touch *t, int n) {
     pthread_mutex_lock(&g_tl);
     int seen[16] = {0};
     for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
         uint32_t id = t[i].id; if (id >= 16) continue;
+        float tx = ui_x(t[i].x), ty = t[i].y;
         seen[id] = 1;
         if (!g_gf[id].down) g_gf[id].pend = 1;
-        g_gf[id].down = 1; g_gf[id].x = t[i].x; g_gf[id].y = t[i].y;
-        if (g_f[id].st == F_LIFTED && g_f[id].reported) { g_f[id].again = 1; g_f[id].ax = t[i].x; g_f[id].ay = t[i].y; continue; }
+        g_gf[id].down = 1; g_gf[id].x = tx; g_gf[id].y = ty;
+        if (g_f[id].st == F_LIFTED && g_f[id].reported) { g_f[id].again = 1; g_f[id].ax = tx; g_f[id].ay = ty; continue; }
         if (g_f[id].st == F_EMPTY) { g_f[id].st = F_DOWN; g_f[id].reported = 0; }
         else if (g_f[id].st == F_LIFTED) g_f[id].st = F_DOWN;              // Pressed again before the lift was reported: treat it as held down all along
-        g_f[id].x = t[i].x; g_f[id].y = t[i].y;
+        g_f[id].x = tx; g_f[id].y = ty;
     }
     for (int id = 0; id < 16; id++) {
         if (!seen[id]) g_gf[id].down = 0;
